==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|ang|bʰruHg}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*brūkaną||to enjoy, use}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*bʰruHg-||enjoy}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|brūka}}, {{cog|osx|brūkan}}, {{cog|odt|*brūkan}}, {{cog|goh|brūhhan}}, {{cog|got|𐌱𐍂𐌿𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root was also the source of Latin {{m|la|fruor||enjoy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|brūcan}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|brūcan}}

# to [[use]]
# to [[harness]], take advantage of, [[employ]], [[exploit]], [[enjoy]]

